menu "Dust mosaic"

    config DUST_SLOT
        int "This screen's place in the wall (0 = choose on screen)"
        range 0 9
        default 0
        help
            1-9, left to right, top to bottom. Leave at 0 to pick it on the screen at first boot
            (tap for the next number, hold to save) or later with the console command "slot N".

    config DUST_CHANNEL
        int "Wi-Fi channel the wall talks on"
        range 1 13
        default 6

    config DUST_GAP_PX
        int "Gap between neighbouring screens' active areas, in pixels"
        range 0 300
        default 148
        help
            Distance between the lit areas of two neighbouring screens, in pixels. The panel is
            480 px across 38.8 mm, so 1 mm is about 12.4 px. With the magnetic sleeves in
            hardware/ that's 2 sleeve walls (2 mm) + 2 fit clearances (0.4 mm) + 2 screen bezels:
            with 3.6 mm bezels, 12 mm, about 148 px.

    config DUST_WALL_EARS
        int "How many tiles on the wall listen for the wake word at once"
        range 1 9
        default 9
        help
            Listening costs each tile some CPU. All nine listening gives the best sense of where
            the speaker is standing; fewer leaves more CPU for drawing. The wall picks the
            centre and corners first and spares the leader when it can. Tiles drawing below
            10 fps stop listening on their own. Lifted tiles always listen for themselves.

    config DUST_WAKE_WORD
        string "Wake word model (esp-sr WakeNet name filter)"
        default "hiesp"
        help
            Part of the WakeNet model name to look for in the model partition: "hiesp" for
            "Hi ESP" (CONFIG_SR_WN_WN9_HIESP). Choose the model itself under ESP Speech
            Recognition in menuconfig. A custom "Hey Dust" needs Espressif's wake word training.

    config DUST_SPEAKER_VOLUME
        int "Speaker volume"
        range 0 100
        default 70

endmenu
